            <div class="one_first first_column">
<table style="width:100%; border:0px solid white; border-collapse:separate" cellpadding="5px" cellspacing="10px">
<tr>
<td>
<img src="Images/richard.jpg" alt=""  /></td>
<td>
<h1>Richard Brady</h1>
<p style="text-align:justify">Richard Brady is Director of Cambridge Legal English Centre and British Legal Centre and supporting Indian Legal Centre in India.</p>
<p style="text-align:justify">His initial career was as a lawyer qualifying in 1976 and then spent 8 years as a police prosecutor in Southern England before leaving to develop his own law practice in London. In 1997 Richard re-qualified as a specialist in Finance and Insurance following his experience of running a client’s medical expenses insurance company in the Middle East. He then spent the next 7 years working in the City of London working in banking and finance.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p style="text-align:justify">In 2005 he decided to leave the City of London and after quickly qualifying as a teacher of English, began to travel around the world. He started to teach legal English and law in Eastern Europe to practising lawyers whom he had met through his law practice. Richard became aware of the opportunities for training and communication offered by new technology and since 2008 he has been the head of the British Legal Centre. </p>
<p style="text-align:justify">Since 2005 Richard has specialized in teaching professional skills to lawyers and other executives in many law and audit companies in Europe and Asia including Ernst & Young, Price Warehouse Cooper’s, Shoenherr’s, Norr Steifenhoffer Lutz, Deloitte and Touche, Baker McKenzie, and Shalakany Law Office and also conducted training at legal departments of many commercial corporations in Europe and Asia. British Legal Centre has built up a strong company presence in Brazil and Egypt and is also a partner of the Deloitte Academy of the Caucuses in Central Asia. Currently BLC courses are being integrated into the Law Degree courses of several leading Universities in the South East Asia and Eastern Europe.</p>
<p style="text-align:justify">Richard has just finished an intensive training course in November 2014, in Cairo, covering Contract management and Risk management for a Nuclear Power Plant Construction company in Egypt and he has been asked to repeat the course in Cairo in 2014 for the Nuclear Power engineers employed by another Middle Eastern Government. Following are the courses offered by him:</p>
<table  style="width:100%">
 <tr>
   <td>
<ul>
 <li>Contract Law Course</li>
 <li>Land and Mortgage Law English</li>
 <li>Intellectual Property English</li>
 <li>Cambridge University Legal English Certificate (ILEC)</li>
 <li>Contract and Legal Document Drafting Course</li>
 <li>Company and Corporate Law</li>
 <li>Legal writing workshop</li>
 <li>Legal Writing Course</li>
 <li>Legal English Vocabulary - Free course</li>
 <li>Oil and Gas law and legal vocabulary</li>
 <li>Arbitration Law and Practice Course</li>
 <li>Persuasive writing for lawyers</li>
</ul></td>
<td><embed width="330" height="220" flashvars="file=http://www.british-legal-centre.com/data/upload/courses/videos/ILEC.flv&amp;image=http://www.british-legal-centre.com/data/upload/courses/images/5.jpg&amp;width=330&amp;height=220" bgcolor="#161616" allowfullscreen="true" quality="high" name="single" id="single" style="undefined" src="http://www.british-legal-centre.com/data/swf/mediaplayer.swf" type="application/x-shockwave-flash"></td>
 </tr>
</table>
<p>To know more about the above courses <b><a href="http://www.british-legal-centre.com/en/courses.html" target="_blank">Click Here</a></b>.</p>
<p><br/></p>
<table style="width:100%; border:0px solid white; border-collapse:separate" cellpadding="5px" cellspacing="10px">
<%--<tr>
<td>
<img src="Images/2.png" alt="" style="width:300px; height:250px" />
</td>
<td>
<h1>Paul Roach</h1>
<p style="text-align:justify">Paul is a qualified practicing solicitor on the Roll of Solicitors of England and Wales who has considerable courtroom experience in the UK. He has been the senior partner of his own law firm He is also a qualified teacher of science and has worked in the Nuclear industry in the UK and also has experience of working in the Middle East. Paul will be taking over responsibility for development of the company in Brazil and Latin America.
</p>
</td>
</tr>--%>
<%--<tr>
<td>
<img src="Images/3.png" alt="" style="width:300px; height:250px" />
</td>
<td>
<h1>Simon Bradshaw</h1>
<p style="text-align:justify">Simon Bradshaw is highly qualified in both law and engineering, with specialist expertise in IT and intellectual property law and extensive experience in technical analysis and project management. Called to the Bar in 2009, he previously worked as an engineering project manager and technology consultant in a variety of roles for the UK Government.
</p>
</td>
</tr>--%>
<tr>
<td>
<img src="Images/Jessica Muckle.jpg" alt=""  />
</td>
<td>
<h1>Jessica Muckle</h1>
<p style="text-align:justify">
After graduating with a BA/LLB degree from Waikato University in 2007 and Professional Legal Studies Course in 2008, Jessica was admitted to the High Court of New Zealand as a Barrister and Solicitor in February 2008. Her presentation, communication and commitment makes an excellent candidate for a role within the legal industry. She has excellent interpersonal skills with a particular interest in front-line people interaction within the legal environment.
</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p><br/></p>
<table style="width:100%; border:0px solid white; border-collapse:separate" cellpadding="5px" cellspacing="10px">
<tr>
<td>
<img src="Images/IRELAND.jpg" alt=""  />
</td>
<td>
<h1>Arran Dowling Hussey</h1>
<p style="text-align:justify">
Arran is a Barrister-at-law, adjudicator, arbitrator and mediator. He co-wrote Arbitration Law (Round Hall, Dublin 2008) which is being revised and the 2nd edition will issue later in 2014. From 2013 he has served on the Board of Management of the Chartered Institute of Arbitrators in London. He is a Door Tenant at Temple Court Chambers in London. 
</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p style="text-align:justify">Since 2004 he has been a part time law lecturer, tutor or guest lecturer for a number of institutions including Dublin City University, Law Society of Ireland, Chartered Institute of Arbitrators, Dublin Institute of Technology and the University of Limerick. He has taught 380 hours at third level since 2004. He is a Fellow of the Chartered Institute of Arbitrators and a member of number of domestic and international arbitral panels. He has contributed around 30 articles to journals such as Global Arbitration Review, The (Irish) Bar Review, Commercial Law Practitioner, Irish Law Times and the Employment Law Reports. He has full rights of audience in the Republic of Ireland and appears regularly in a range of courts in both civil and criminal matters. He has been a member of the Refugee Legal Service Panel of Barristers since 2004, a member of the Office of the Director of Corporate Enforcement's Legal Panel since 2008 and later that year also joined the Department of Defense's Legal Aid Panel.
</p>
<p><br/></p>
<table style="width:100%; border:0px solid white; border-collapse:separate" cellpadding="5px" cellspacing="10px">
<tr>
<td>
<img width="150" height="150" src="Images/mcharles.jpg" alt=""  />
</td>
<td>
<h1>Mikhail A.X. Charles</h1>
<p style="text-align:justify">
Mikhail is a ﻿Barrister & Solicitor​ in General criminal and commercial practice at the English & Welsh (non-practising), Vincentian, Grenadian and St. Lucian Bars with particular interests in corporate law and financial crime and also a Contributor in Laws of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines. He is currently working in Baptiste & Co. Law Firm Inc. as a Specialist in Corporate and Advisory Practice. He is a Qualified and Licensed Real Estate Valuer in Saint Vincent and the Grenadines.
</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p><br/></p>
<table style="width:100%; border:0px solid white; border-collapse:separate" cellpadding="5px" cellspacing="10px">
<tr>
<td>
<img width="140" height="180" src="Images/jia.jpg" alt=""  />
</td>
<td>
<h1>Shengnan Jia </h1>
<p style="text-align:justify">
Shengnan is a practicing lawyer in Civil Commercial Law in China Managing the international business team and expanding the business overseas, Providing legal advice for clients who are seeking to invest overseas and Assisting Chinese clients to negotiate with international clients. She has experience in litigation, participated and disposed of Commercial Maritime Law and disputes on Mortgage, Loan Guarantee of Banking and Financing, Bank Acceptances, Guarantee of Trust Loan, Deposit Certificate, Transfer of Creditor’s Right, Shareholder’s Interest, Enterprise Reorganization and Restructuring, etc. in the Supreme People’s Court of the People’s Republic of China and some Higher Courts. 
</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p style="text-align:justify">
She is a Member of All-China Bar Association and Professional Committee of Maritime Law of Beijing Municipal Lawyers Association. She received many Awards and Honours such as Excellent Lawyer, Beijing Beidou Dingming Law Firm, 2008; Advanced Lawyer for Legal Aid, Beijing Chaoyang Bureau of Justice, 2008; Excellent Lawyer of Party Member, Beijing Chaoyang District, 2009,2010 etc. She published articles on Legal Issues Pertaining to Dormant Partner in Journal of Science & Times (Jan. 2006, P56-58) and Analysis on the handling of cases involving standard terms in the trial with regard to an agency agreement in Journal of Science & Times (May 2008, P53-57).
</p>
